  "id": "modularity",
  "term": "modularity",
  "definition": "Modularity is a network measure of how much a system is divided into separate clusters or subgroups rather than being broadly interconnected. In lexical-semantic networks, higher modularity indicates a more fragmented and less integrated organization.",
